<LegalLayout title="Non-Discrimination Notice" description="Neuhaus Foot & Ankle follows civil rights laws and provides language and communication help at no cost.">
  <p>
    Neuhaus Foot &amp; Ankle follows federal civil rights laws. We do not discriminate against, exclude or treat
    people differently because of race, color, national origin, age, disability or sex.
  </p>

  <h2>Free help for you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Qualified sign language interpreters and written information in other formats, such as large print, for people with disabilities.</li>
    <li>Language services for people whose first language is not English, including qualified interpreters and information in other languages.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To ask for these services, call any of our offices. There is no cost to you.</p>

  <h2>If you feel you were treated unfairly</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe we did not provide these services or treated you differently for any of the reasons above, you can
    file a complaint with us. Please call or visit any office and ask for our Privacy or Compliance Officer. We
    will help you file it.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also file a civil rights complaint with the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Office for
    Civil Rights, online at
    <a class="underline" href="https://ocrportal.hhs.gov/ocr/portal/lobby.jsf" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ocrportal.hhs.gov</a>
    or by phone at 1-800-368-1019 (TTY 1-800-537-7697).
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
